1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,510
[Disclaimer: All events
depicted in this series are fictional]

2
00:00:01,530 --> 00:00:02,340
[and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,250
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:22,020
Khwankhao

5
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:23,820
took her friends from Bangkok
trekking in the forest,

6
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,260
but it's been three days now.

7
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:26,330
Still no sign of them.

8
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,600
I'll be back as soon as I can.

9
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:29,820
I thought Paran was gonna turn down work

10
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:32,090
after the monk warned him
about the misfortune coming his way.

11
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,420
This misfortune hanging over you

12
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,090
is grave enough to cost you your life.

13
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,350
What should we do, Khem?

14
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:37,510
Should we help Master instead?

15
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:38,470
We should go to the set.

16
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,260
They're waiting for our help, too.

17
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,540
Those kids are being hunted
by malicious spirits

18
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:46,280
that are thralls of a sorcerer.

19
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,960
Please grant me the chance

20
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:50,990
to return to my beloved.

21
00:00:54,530 --> 00:01:17,650
[Incanting]

22
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:22,990
Those brats...

23
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:24,110
Where the hell did they go?

24
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:50,210
You alright, Max?

25
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:52,720
I'm good.

26
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:54,410
What about you, Pleng?

27
00:01:54,670 --> 00:01:55,479
Are you okay?

28
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,210
I'm fine. I'm not as badly hurt as you are.

29
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:04,200
Khao, hanging in there?

30
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,980
The Seven-Layer Crystal Wall spell

31
00:02:28,010 --> 00:02:30,050
is still masking our presence
from those spirits.

32
00:02:30,329 --> 00:02:31,710
Let's catch our breath while we can.

33
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:53,350
♪ A blessed day has come,
with fortune aglow ♪

34
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:59,430
♪ Graceful offerings
are arranged in a row ♪

35
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:03,680
♪ Sacred threads and rings of gold, ♪

36
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,580
♪ Jewels and necklaces,
precious to behold ♪

37
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,820
♪ A feast overflowing
with plenty to spare ♪

38
00:03:08,850 --> 00:03:11,660
♪ All things prepared
with the greatest care ♪

39
00:03:11,690 --> 00:03:14,230
♪ Betel rolls and areca nuts
are laid there ♪

40
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:17,230
♪ Everything adorned
and displayed with flair ♪

41
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:23,300
♪ "May your vital forces come forth" ♪

42
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:27,430
♪ May your vital forces come forth ♪

43
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:31,710
♪ O vital forces, beyond the skies, ♪

44
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:33,950
♪ In distant realms
where your souls fly, ♪

45
00:03:33,970 --> 00:03:35,770
♪ Heed the call and now arise, ♪

46
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:42,600
♪ Return to where your vessels lie ♪

47
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,290
Here you go.

48
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:33,020
Thanks.

49
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:38,540
Here.

50
00:04:40,909 --> 00:04:41,750
Thanks.

51
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:44,420
- Spitting image.
- Spitting image.

52
00:04:58,650 --> 00:05:00,520
You drink the exact same thing as me.

53
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:02,920
Bold and aromatic.

54
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,490
It tastes like freshly brewed coffee.

55
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,510
I could stay up
busting ghosts all night with this.

56
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:15,500
Could I ask for your advice on something?

57
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,690
Sure.

58
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,450
I was wondering,

59
00:05:19,470 --> 00:05:23,370
since you've been seeing ghosts your whole life,

60
00:05:23,450 --> 00:05:25,910
you wouldn't be scared of them anymore, right?

61
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,480
You'd only fear spirits that mean harm.

62
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:30,670
Exactly.

63
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:33,650
You really did your homework.

64
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:41,680
Frost, didn't you have a question for Jet?

65
00:05:43,470 --> 00:05:44,380
Go ahead.

66
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,120
Oh...

67
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:46,690
Right.

68
00:05:47,659 --> 00:05:49,590
Well, the catering lady just taught me this,

69
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:52,810
so I'd like you to check
if my accent is alright.

70
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,290
"I miss Master so much."

71
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,210
Whoa.

72
00:05:59,950 --> 00:06:01,520
Why are you so adorable?

73
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,470
Stop it, Tol.

74
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:09,530
- You're exactly like us...
- You're exactly like us...

75
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:12,910
Hello, Khem.

76
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:15,470
Sorry, I was dealing with the art department.

77
00:06:16,030 --> 00:06:17,240
Sorry to keep you waiting.

78
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:21,450
Coach Dol,

79
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,450
that's Namprung over there.

80
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:30,760
- Hi, Coach Dol.
- Hello, Khem.

81
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:32,050
Hi, guys.

82
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:34,600
Identical.

83
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:36,760
Wait.

84
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:40,340
King, Namprung, Tol, Frost.

85
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:42,750
Why aren't you in costume yet, babes?

86
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,020
Get changed so we can roll

87
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:45,330
while we still have time.

88
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,390
If we cancel another shoot,
I'm gonna lose it.

89
00:06:47,659 --> 00:06:48,760
Move now.

90
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,050
Go on.

91
00:06:52,730 --> 00:06:55,700
Let's go over our lines
while getting our hair and makeup done, King.

92
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:57,980
I've already memorized mine.

93
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,920
I feel bad for the crew.

94
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:01,840
We've called off this scene multiple times,

95
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:03,560
so I want to wrap it up fast.

96
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:13,980
Poor guys. It's their debut series,
and nothing is going smoothly.

97
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:18,190
I hope this series blows up for them.

98
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:20,810
Anyway,

99
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:22,750
thanks for coming to help.

100
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:24,210
We're happy to help.

101
00:07:24,410 --> 00:07:26,670
Could you walk us through

102
00:07:26,690 --> 00:07:27,970
everything that happened?

103
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:43,290
The location department
usually preps the site in advance.

104
00:07:43,909 --> 00:07:46,240
That day, everyone happened to show up late.

105
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,380
Where are you guys?

106
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:04,150
Hey, you're supposed to be here first.

107
00:08:04,430 --> 00:08:05,020
Oh...

108
00:08:57,880 --> 00:09:01,110
After that, everyone went to
a temple to make merit.

109
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,860
We thought that'd be the end of it.

110
00:09:03,930 --> 00:09:05,250
Turns out,

111
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:07,980
it only got worse.

112
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:09,310
Cut.

113
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:13,650
Hey, you're the ghost here.

114
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:15,680
You're supposed to scare Khem,

115
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:19,160
not jump at every rustling bush.

116
00:09:19,190 --> 00:09:22,060
Coach Dol, I think I saw something
on the left side of Camera A's frame.

117
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:23,360
Kin, play it back.

118
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,900
- On it.
- Right at the end.

119
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:25,810
What is it?

120
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:26,930
The very end.

121
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,520
What now?

122
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:29,890
Keep rewinding.

123
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:34,410
- Left where? You mean... Whoa.
- There.

124
00:09:34,430 --> 00:09:35,480
Right there.

125
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:36,670
Wait, hold on.

126
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,000
Shit.

127
00:09:45,850 --> 00:09:47,210
[It's always me]

128
00:09:47,230 --> 00:09:48,080
That's what happened.

129
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,350
When we played it back again,

130
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:51,540
it was gone.

131
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:58,020
Pardon me for speaking up,

132
00:09:58,850 --> 00:09:59,700
but...

133
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:01,570
I've had this strange feeling

134
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:04,140
ever since we got here.

135
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:06,800
Have you considered changing locations?

136
00:10:06,870 --> 00:10:09,040
We'd miss our air date.

137
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:12,930
We were planning to ask the monks
at the nearby temple for help.

138
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,890
You know, the one we visited to make merit.

139
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:16,720
But once we went there again,

140
00:10:18,010 --> 00:10:19,490
it was completely abandoned.

141
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,690
Jet, can you handle this?

142
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:30,800
Yeah.

143
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,420
Coach Dol,

144
00:11:14,210 --> 00:11:15,640
we had an agreement.

145
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:18,140
All the cast and crew

146
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,900
were supposed to wait at the base camp.

147
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:26,580
Come on, I asked you all to come here.

148
00:11:26,610 --> 00:11:29,430
How could I leave you on your own?

149
00:11:29,450 --> 00:11:30,730
Besides,

150
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:33,440
the cast is already here,

151
00:11:33,470 --> 00:11:35,380
so they might as well watch the ritual.

152
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:38,260
It'll help them get into character for the scenes.

153
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:39,210
Right?

154
00:11:39,230 --> 00:11:42,520
I promise we'll stay quiet and out of the way.

155
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:49,200
Jet, it's the auspicious hour.

156
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:52,820
Gather in close.

157
00:11:54,610 --> 00:11:56,390
Focus your minds, everyone.

158
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:39,100
[Incanting]

159
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,620
Will you not leave us be?

160
00:13:18,910 --> 00:13:19,670
Elder,

161
00:13:21,190 --> 00:13:24,060
we only seek your permission
to film a series here.

162
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:27,990
We will dedicate merit to you in return.

163
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:08,080
He's gone.

164
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,960
The other spirits are also gone.

165
00:14:11,830 --> 00:14:13,430
But isn't it strange?

166
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,200
Why was it so easy?

167
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:21,270
Isn't easy a good thing?

168
00:14:21,810 --> 00:14:23,710
It means my craft is still sharp.

169
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,100
I really asked the right person.

170
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,000
Thank you so much.

171
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:35,340
Let's go.

172
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,460
Pack it up.

173
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:37,690
Alright.

174
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:38,360
Brilliant.

175
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,500
Come on, guys. Get ready.

176
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:44,510
Lighting and art department, head onto the set.

177
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,650
Let's wrap early today, babes.

178
00:14:47,010 --> 00:14:48,090
Come on.

179
00:14:48,590 --> 00:14:51,100
We're going home early, babes.

180
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:07,330
Hold on.

181
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,550
Has anyone seen Coach Dol?

182
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,140
Shit. We're in trouble.

183
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:30,490
Look at this.

184
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:53,670
Guys...

185
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:14,560
[K-2101 Bangkok]

186
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,570
The call won't go through.

187
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:18,170
Master must still be in the forest.

188
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:20,530
Give him time.

189
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,850
He promised he'd contact us.

190
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:29,260
Khem.

191
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,760
What are you seeing now?

192
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:52,860
Is something wrong?

193
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:18,180
You cleared that graveyard out thoroughly.

194
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:21,190
Naturally. That's my expertise.

195
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:24,849
Wait.

196
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,240
A graveyard?

197
00:17:27,970 --> 00:17:29,360
This place is a graveyard?

198
00:17:30,390 --> 00:17:31,800
Nobody mentioned that.

199
00:17:34,810 --> 00:17:35,760
It used to be.

200
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:40,070
Most of the spirits here are unclaimed,

201
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:41,990
but they mean no harm.

202
00:17:42,670 --> 00:17:44,180
Perhaps they were given proper funeral rites

203
00:17:44,210 --> 00:17:46,950
by an undertaker with spiritual knowledge.

204
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:51,630
If you were minding your own business,

205
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:54,030
and someone evicted you from your home,

206
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,070
how would you feel?

207
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:01,100
Those spirits have gathered elsewhere now.

208
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,540
The reason Charn can't trace Coach Dol's presence

209
00:18:05,550 --> 00:18:07,410
is that multiple spirits

210
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,440
are cloaking his life force.

211
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:13,690
Focus your minds

212
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:17,200
toward where those spirits have gathered,

213
00:18:18,090 --> 00:18:19,190
and you'll find him.

214
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:27,740
How are things on your end?

215
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:30,560
You're here in spirit form,

216
00:18:30,990 --> 00:18:33,060
so that means
you're still in the border forest, right?

217
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,170
Yeah.

218
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:36,830
I am.

219
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:43,280
I've managed to help some of them.

220
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:45,360
Don't worry.

221
00:18:45,650 --> 00:18:46,920
How can I not worry?

222
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:52,760
I already know

223
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,470
about Monk Kasem's warning.

224
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:58,220
Since when

225
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,810
did you start keeping secrets from me?

226
00:19:07,730 --> 00:19:09,490
I shouldn't have let you take this job.

227
00:19:15,510 --> 00:19:16,500
I'm sorry.

228
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,380
But I'm glad I listened to you.

229
00:19:24,090 --> 00:19:25,510
If I hadn't stepped in,

230
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:29,280
even more lives would have been lost.

231
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,630
Once I'm done here,

232
00:19:46,650 --> 00:19:48,500
I'll come back to you as soon as I can.

233
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:58,720
I promised you

234
00:20:00,230 --> 00:20:01,790
I'd make it back alive.

235
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:06,370
I always keep my promises.

236
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,870
You know that.

237
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,900
Why don't you get out of here first?

238
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:50,760
Come on.

239
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:53,800
We can't.

240
00:20:54,230 --> 00:20:55,440
Oh, okay.

241
00:20:55,910 --> 00:20:57,580
Then... drink some water.

242
00:20:57,610 --> 00:20:58,760
It'll help you feel refreshed.

243
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,790
Then we can figure out what to do next.

244
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:03,230
I want to help them...

245
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:05,720
We need to save Max.

246
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:09,260
We don't even know where he is now.

247
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,320
We kept going in circles.

248
00:21:14,650 --> 00:21:15,590
Master,

249
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,800
the kids refuse to leave.

250
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:20,520
They want us to find their friends first,

251
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:22,300
or they won't leave.

252
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,510
Give me your wrist.

253
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,430
Come on.

254
00:21:48,210 --> 00:21:49,060
Give me your wrist.

255
00:21:58,020 --> 00:21:58,850
I know

256
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,510
you're scared out of your minds.

257
00:22:02,290 --> 00:22:04,060
If you want your friends to survive,

258
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:05,600
pull yourselves together.

259
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:09,910
Your testimony is what will save them.

260
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:16,840
Come on.

261
00:22:17,350 --> 00:22:18,310
Up on your feet.

262
00:22:27,030 --> 00:22:27,740
So,

263
00:22:28,850 --> 00:22:30,820
can you tell us

264
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:34,620
how you got lost so deep in this forest?

265
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,620
When Pond came to drive us home,

266
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:48,660
we asked him to pull over so we could pee.

267
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:51,710
Max came along with us.

268
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:53,200
Then, out of nowhere,

269
00:22:53,230 --> 00:22:55,040
he heard something strange
and went to check.

270
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,700
When we realized

271
00:22:58,470 --> 00:23:00,210
he'd been gone for too long,

272
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:03,700
we all went in after him.

273
00:23:06,330 --> 00:23:07,150
Quit whining.

274
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:09,970
Move it.

275
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:12,540
Walk.

276
00:23:12,630 --> 00:23:13,460
Keep moving.

277
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:14,940
- Hey.
- Get up.

278
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,540
- Get up and move.
- Move.

279
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:17,080
Get up.

280
00:23:20,250 --> 00:23:21,260
Max, what are you filming?

281
00:23:21,290 --> 00:23:21,950
Shit.

282
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:23,070
What?

283
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,830
Max...

284
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:26,320
- Hey.
- Get up.

285
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:27,400
- Get up and move.
- Move.

286
00:23:27,420 --> 00:23:29,240
- Max...
- Max.

287
00:23:29,270 --> 00:23:31,450
Shit, is this human trafficking?

288
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:32,320
Shit.

289
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,480
- Hey, what's your problem?
- This is human trafficking,

290
00:23:34,510 --> 00:23:36,570
not some petty gambling. Knock it off, man.

291
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,340
Yeah, drop it before we all get screwed.

292
00:23:38,370 --> 00:23:40,430
Guys, if we do nothing,

293
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:42,080
we're no better than them.

294
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:43,570
- It's not your job to do this.
- This is no time to play the hero.

295
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:45,340
- I'm taking this footage to the police.
- Max, come on...

296
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:47,810
Guys, you done yet?
Back in the car.

297
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:49,830
Hey.

298
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:52,860
Who's that?

299
00:23:53,510 --> 00:23:54,330
Shit.

300
00:23:57,070 --> 00:23:57,880
Shit.

301
00:23:57,910 --> 00:23:59,020
Run!

302
00:23:59,660 --> 00:24:00,460
Stop.

303
00:24:00,490 --> 00:24:01,550
Don't follow them.

304
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:29,250
[Incanting]

305
00:25:02,510 --> 00:25:03,380
Baitong...

306
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:15,690
Pond,

307
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,370
missing your wife?

308
00:25:26,590 --> 00:25:27,320
Yeah.

309
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,920
She's pregnant, too.

310
00:25:51,270 --> 00:25:53,430
If I don't make it out of here tonight,

311
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:59,710
could you give Baitong this ring?

312
00:26:03,530 --> 00:26:04,850
Come on, man.

313
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:09,730
Give it to her yourself.

314
00:26:11,330 --> 00:26:12,850
We're making it out of here together.

315
00:26:23,610 --> 00:26:25,280
Come here. Bring it in.

316
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:28,050
Pond, come on.

317
00:26:31,310 --> 00:26:32,930
- Pond.
- Come on.

318
00:26:37,780 --> 00:26:38,720
Come on, man.

319
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,770
- Watch the wound.
- Sorry.

320
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,000
By tomorrow morning,

321
00:26:49,230 --> 00:26:50,590
we'll make it out together.

322
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:00,730
Coach Dol is somewhere here,

323
00:27:00,910 --> 00:27:02,440
but his soul is fading.

324
00:27:03,650 --> 00:27:04,630
Follow me.

325
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:20,300
It's pretty creepy here.

326
00:27:21,910 --> 00:27:24,180
This feels like a test of courage

327
00:27:24,430 --> 00:27:26,120
in those childhood cartoons.

328
00:27:36,180 --> 00:27:37,780
Yeah, just think of it

329
00:27:38,130 --> 00:27:40,460
as one of those cartoons we used to watch.

330
00:27:40,710 --> 00:27:41,430
Right?

331
00:27:41,550 --> 00:27:43,330
What cartoon has ghosts
right in your face like this?

332
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,020
Jet!

333
00:27:44,610 --> 00:27:47,040
Must be nice being grounded and seeing nothing.

334
00:27:48,770 --> 00:27:49,680
Stop talking.

335
00:27:57,010 --> 00:27:57,870
Coach Dol...

336
00:27:58,760 --> 00:27:59,760
- Coach Dol?
- Oh...

337
00:28:03,450 --> 00:28:04,680
[It's always me]

338
00:28:04,700 --> 00:28:05,730
Coach Dol!

339
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:24,290
How many of them are here?

340
00:28:24,450 --> 00:28:25,750
I can hardly breathe.

341
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,150
Whoa...

342
00:28:29,620 --> 00:28:30,520
At least a dozen.

343
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:33,300
Don't worry.

344
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,590
I'll handle them.

345
00:28:36,630 --> 00:28:37,640
Wait, Jet.

346
00:28:38,100 --> 00:28:40,170
- What?
- Remember what Master told us?

347
00:28:46,180 --> 00:28:47,910
Took you long enough.

348
00:28:54,870 --> 00:28:56,150
Who are you, Elder?

349
00:28:58,130 --> 00:28:59,710
I was this temple's undertaker.

350
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:01,660
I've cremated hundreds

351
00:29:01,690 --> 00:29:03,180
and buried thousands.

352
00:29:03,740 --> 00:29:06,690
Made merit for every unclaimed body.

353
00:29:07,510 --> 00:29:08,640
I entered their dreams

354
00:29:08,670 --> 00:29:10,440
and haunted their set,

355
00:29:10,630 --> 00:29:11,980
yet they still wouldn't leave.

356
00:29:12,270 --> 00:29:13,570
We were minding our own business,

357
00:29:13,660 --> 00:29:15,840
and you came stomping all over the place,

358
00:29:15,860 --> 00:29:17,120
making a racket.

359
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:21,900
We're here to apologize on the crew's behalf.

360
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:25,180
Nobody meant any disrespect.

361
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,630
Please let our director go.

362
00:29:28,660 --> 00:29:30,300
Your director's the worst one.

363
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:32,060
Everyone else was ready to pack up,

364
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:34,240
but he kept refusing to leave,

365
00:29:34,260 --> 00:29:35,460
whining about missing the air date.

366
00:29:36,790 --> 00:29:38,040
Come on, Elder.

367
00:29:38,790 --> 00:29:41,280
We already asked for permission.

368
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:43,630
Cut us some slack, please.

369
00:29:43,660 --> 00:29:44,460
Jet!

370
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,540
Just because you asked doesn't mean you get it.

371
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:53,560
What are they trying to do?

372
00:29:58,200 --> 00:29:59,710
To all the unclaimed spirits here,

373
00:30:00,930 --> 00:30:01,950
please...

374
00:30:02,260 --> 00:30:03,520
let me help you.

375
00:30:03,870 --> 00:30:05,320
Please.

376
00:30:20,390 --> 00:30:21,400
Malatang?

377
00:30:21,430 --> 00:30:22,220
Sure thing.

378
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:24,340
I'll have the crew offer alms for you.

379
00:30:24,830 --> 00:30:26,650
Yeah, thank you.

380
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:33,140
Hotpot?

381
00:30:33,170 --> 00:30:33,960
You got it.

382
00:30:33,990 --> 00:30:36,130
I'll have the crew offer that with the alms.

383
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:52,590
He's only asleep,

384
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:54,280
but lingering among us for too long

385
00:30:54,300 --> 00:30:56,200
isn't good for the living.

386
00:30:56,780 --> 00:30:58,720
How you revive him is your concern.

387
00:30:59,510 --> 00:31:00,340
So...

388
00:31:01,140 --> 00:31:03,300
is there anything we can do for you?

389
00:31:03,330 --> 00:31:04,150
No.

390
00:31:04,510 --> 00:31:06,150
All I want is peace.

391
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:07,630
Come daybreak,

392
00:31:08,250 --> 00:31:09,620
pack up and leave.

393
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:13,690
Thank you.

394
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:28,510
Slow down, Khao.

395
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:30,080
You holding up?

396
00:31:31,570 --> 00:31:32,370
Wait...

397
00:31:33,150 --> 00:31:35,590
Isn't that where we came in?

398
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:36,880
Did we make it?

399
00:31:36,910 --> 00:31:37,710
Hold on.

400
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:40,480
Something feels off.

401
00:31:41,140 --> 00:31:42,480
It's way too quiet.

402
00:31:42,670 --> 00:31:44,260
Not even a bird is chirping.

403
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:47,400
Should we go back to where we were?

404
00:31:49,570 --> 00:31:50,240
No.

405
00:31:50,930 --> 00:31:51,960
I say we keep going.

406
00:31:52,370 --> 00:31:53,460
Max's wound is too bad.

407
00:31:54,820 --> 00:32:01,080
[Incanting]

408
00:32:01,100 --> 00:32:01,580
Max.

409
00:32:01,610 --> 00:32:02,810
- Hey.
- Max!

410
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:04,380
- Max...
- Max.

411
00:32:04,410 --> 00:32:07,470
Khao, what do we do?

412
00:32:07,500 --> 00:32:08,740
Khao!

413
00:32:08,990 --> 00:32:09,830
Shit.

414
00:32:09,860 --> 00:32:15,170
[Incanting]

415
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:15,930
Max.

416
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:19,060
[Incanting]

417
00:32:21,380 --> 00:32:22,170
Khao!

418
00:32:22,360 --> 00:32:23,290
Khao...

419
00:32:28,670 --> 00:32:40,450
[Incanting]

420
00:32:51,400 --> 00:33:11,880
[Incanting]

421
00:33:17,990 --> 00:33:18,910
Stop.

422
00:33:24,350 --> 00:33:24,990
Max...

423
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:28,190
Unless you want to suffer the same fate,

424
00:33:29,010 --> 00:33:30,410
go back to where you belong,

425
00:33:31,390 --> 00:33:33,270
and I shall release your soul.

426
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:52,170
Guys!

427
00:33:52,190 --> 00:33:53,180
Hang in there.

428
00:33:53,210 --> 00:33:54,430
Hey!

429
00:33:56,790 --> 00:33:57,550
- How are you?
- Hey.

430
00:33:57,580 --> 00:33:58,090
You okay?

431
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,790
- Max can't take it.
- Hang in there, Max.

432
00:33:59,900 --> 00:34:00,790
Max.

433
00:34:01,730 --> 00:34:03,040
I'm right here.

434
00:34:03,070 --> 00:34:04,040
Hang in there.

435
00:34:04,070 --> 00:34:05,650
Stay with us. We're right here.

436
00:34:05,670 --> 00:34:06,570
Calm down.

437
00:34:07,150 --> 00:34:08,960
Stay with me! Look at me, keep looking at me!

438
00:34:54,010 --> 00:34:54,920
We're safe.

439
00:34:57,290 --> 00:34:58,150
We made it.

440
00:34:58,610 --> 00:34:59,780
We're going home.

441
00:35:00,100 --> 00:35:00,900
We're safe.

442
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:03,660
- Easy.
- Up you go.

443
00:35:03,990 --> 00:35:04,720
Okay.

444
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:09,090
- Great.
- Okay.

445
00:35:10,290 --> 00:35:11,500
- Hang on.
- Take a deep breath.

446
00:35:11,530 --> 00:35:13,010
Lean on me.

447
00:35:13,430 --> 00:35:14,710
Easy, alright.

448
00:35:18,300 --> 00:35:19,490
Thank you, Master.

449
00:35:20,340 --> 00:35:22,070
Make sure to bathe in holy water
when you get home.

450
00:35:22,640 --> 00:35:24,300
We're going home, guys.

451
00:35:26,220 --> 00:35:27,280
We're finally going home.

452
00:35:34,950 --> 00:35:35,820
Master!

453
00:35:51,890 --> 00:35:54,310
Make sure you have the doctor examine you again.

454
00:35:55,950 --> 00:35:57,760
- Okay.
- Take good care of yourself.

455
00:35:59,190 --> 00:36:00,640
Goodbye.

456
00:36:05,410 --> 00:36:07,630
Do I really have to do all this
for those ghosts?

457
00:36:08,710 --> 00:36:09,760
I'm counting on you.

458
00:36:11,710 --> 00:36:13,860
Alright, thanks so much either way.

459
00:36:14,340 --> 00:36:14,940
- See you.
- Take care.

460
00:36:14,970 --> 00:36:15,510
Bye.

461
00:36:37,060 --> 00:36:38,480
What's wrong, Khem?

462
00:36:44,850 --> 00:36:45,690
It's just...

463
00:36:47,310 --> 00:36:48,550
My heart is racing.

464
00:36:50,030 --> 00:36:52,820
I have this weird feeling I can't explain.

465
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,370
You barely got any sleep

466
00:36:57,140 --> 00:36:58,740
and drank all that coffee.

467
00:36:59,690 --> 00:37:01,010
Of course your heart is racing.

468
00:37:04,310 --> 00:37:05,270
That's not the reason.

469
00:37:06,930 --> 00:37:07,910
What's with you guys?

470
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:12,030
Master...

471
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:14,100
I sense that he's...

472
00:37:29,350 --> 00:37:30,200
Master!

473
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:43,410
Pierced right through enchanted skin.

474
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:45,490
This sorcerer's bullets

475
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:46,570
actually work.

476
00:37:49,370 --> 00:37:50,650
Thanks, Master,

477
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:52,910
for tracking down these kids for us.

478
00:37:56,820 --> 00:38:02,060
[Incanting]

479
00:38:02,090 --> 00:38:03,240
- It burns...
- It's burning hot...

480
00:38:03,270 --> 00:38:09,800
[Incanting]

481
00:38:12,010 --> 00:38:14,360
Still got fight in you, huh?

482
00:38:14,600 --> 00:38:15,760
In that case,

483
00:38:17,820 --> 00:38:19,820
I'll finish you off first.

484
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,110
First blood!

485
00:38:38,350 --> 00:38:39,300
Stop right there!

486
00:38:40,100 --> 00:38:40,760
Hey, stop.

487
00:38:40,780 --> 00:38:41,560
Stop!

488
00:38:41,590 --> 00:38:42,540
- Hey!
- Freeze.

489
00:38:47,470 --> 00:38:49,050
Surprise, baby.

490
00:38:50,700 --> 00:38:51,840
Get up.

491
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:56,490
I missed you, bro.

492
00:38:56,510 --> 00:38:57,840
Ow, that hurts.

493
00:38:58,710 --> 00:39:00,400
Takes me back to our vocational school days.

494
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,080
Without me,

495
00:39:02,100 --> 00:39:03,650
you wouldn't have made it once again.

496
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:05,760
You're late,
and you're still trying to look cool?

497
00:39:05,930 --> 00:39:06,770
Come on.

498
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:08,800
If not for me,

499
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:11,260
who else could've tracked you down, bro?

500
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:13,360
Those marks you made on the trees

501
00:39:13,390 --> 00:39:15,490
were as faint as cat scratches.

502
00:39:21,670 --> 00:39:22,440
You...

503
00:39:22,670 --> 00:39:23,480
Go to hell.

504
00:39:23,780 --> 00:39:24,230
Shit.

505
00:39:24,260 --> 00:39:27,280
Stop!

506
00:39:48,790 --> 00:39:51,420
Hey, you're still worried, Khem?

507
00:39:53,950 --> 00:39:55,200
I believe

508
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:58,400
the ancestral spirits will watch over Master.

509
00:40:07,650 --> 00:40:09,770
You trust him anyway.

510
00:40:11,060 --> 00:40:12,120
No matter what,

511
00:40:12,440 --> 00:40:13,670
he'll be safe

512
00:40:13,700 --> 00:40:15,640
and come back to marry you.

513
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:39,560
Peem?

514
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:41,740
Peem...

515
00:40:48,220 --> 00:40:49,150
Peem.

516
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:52,890
Peem!

517
00:40:57,650 --> 00:40:58,390
Is this...

518
00:40:58,950 --> 00:41:00,110
really you?

519
00:41:00,310 --> 00:41:01,240
You're not a ghost, are you?

520
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:02,790
Is this your spirit form?

521
00:41:02,810 --> 00:41:05,570
Why are you covered in so many wounds?

522
00:41:05,600 --> 00:41:08,000
Are you alright? What about...

523
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,130
I'm back.

524
00:41:31,220 --> 00:41:32,800
Hi, I'm back.

525
00:41:33,620 --> 00:41:35,070
Coming all the way here, huh?

526
00:41:35,370 --> 00:41:37,570
Yeah, just a phone call would do.

527
00:41:37,810 --> 00:41:38,650
Sorry.

528
00:41:38,820 --> 00:41:39,690
My phone died.

529
00:41:39,950 --> 00:41:42,250
Someone insisted
on catching the first flight out,

530
00:41:42,280 --> 00:41:43,930
refusing to even see a doctor.

531
00:41:44,470 --> 00:41:46,000
Down so bad, it's ridiculous.

532
00:41:47,510 --> 00:41:49,090
More wounds?

533
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:53,190
At least let me know what you're doing.

534
00:41:56,260 --> 00:41:58,400
How did you even end up with these?

535
00:42:01,300 --> 00:42:01,790
Go to hell.

536
00:42:01,820 --> 00:42:03,300
Stop!

537
00:42:18,680 --> 00:42:19,880
I told you to stop.

538
00:42:20,330 --> 00:42:22,650
Paran has protective tattoos
that make him impervious to blades.

539
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:30,810
Stop.

540
00:42:35,060 --> 00:42:35,910
That's enough.

541
00:42:39,770 --> 00:42:41,500
Don't burden your soul with more sins.

542
00:43:26,250 --> 00:43:27,400
Thank you.

543
00:43:29,070 --> 00:43:31,380
May you journey to a peaceful realm.

544
00:43:36,890 --> 00:43:38,600
Let your karma guide your way.

545
00:43:56,590 --> 00:43:57,450
Hello.

546
00:43:58,940 --> 00:43:59,840
You got lucky.

547
00:44:02,280 --> 00:44:03,230
We made it.

548
00:44:04,330 --> 00:44:05,130
We're safe.

549
00:44:05,300 --> 00:44:06,590
Watch his wound.

550
00:44:07,160 --> 00:44:08,250
- I...
- We're going home.

551
00:44:08,280 --> 00:44:10,040
I won't go on another trip
with you guys again.

552
00:44:10,730 --> 00:44:12,340
- Let's go!
- Stay awake!

553
00:44:18,130 --> 00:44:19,230
What are you laughing at?

554
00:44:19,260 --> 00:44:20,770
Cut it out.

555
00:44:20,790 --> 00:44:22,040
If you don't, I'll laugh, too.

556
00:44:28,770 --> 00:44:29,600
Move!

557
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:30,520
Keep walking!

558
00:44:30,550 --> 00:44:31,250
Move!

559
00:44:31,430 --> 00:44:32,290
It's over now.

560
00:44:35,540 --> 00:44:36,790
Time to go home.

561
00:44:38,060 --> 00:44:39,260
Your parents must be worried sick.

562
00:44:43,860 --> 00:44:44,850
Look at Pond.

563
00:44:46,490 --> 00:44:47,900
He must be exhausted.

564
00:44:48,610 --> 00:44:49,580
Wake up.

565
00:44:49,600 --> 00:44:50,110
Pond.

566
00:44:50,140 --> 00:44:51,250
It's all over.

567
00:44:51,420 --> 00:44:52,780
- Pond.
- Pond.

568
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:54,360
Hey, Pond.

569
00:44:59,460 --> 00:45:00,200
Shit.

570
00:45:01,520 --> 00:45:02,430
What's wrong with him?

571
00:45:02,830 --> 00:45:03,840
He's been shot.

572
00:45:04,810 --> 00:45:05,290
Pond...

573
00:45:05,320 --> 00:45:06,320
- What happened?
- Pond.

574
00:45:06,350 --> 00:45:07,470
- Pond.
- Hey.

575
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:08,540
Pond!

576
00:45:08,560 --> 00:45:09,930
- Pond, what happened to you?
- Wake up.

577
00:45:09,950 --> 00:45:11,470
- Come on, wake up.
- Pond...

578
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:12,570
- Pond, hey.
- Talk to me.

579
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,320
- What happened to him?
- Pond, wake up.

580
00:45:15,870 --> 00:45:18,510
- Master, what happened to him?
- Pond.

581
00:45:18,530 --> 00:45:19,980
- Hey, press on the wound.
- Why is he like this?

582
00:45:20,010 --> 00:45:22,230
- Master...
- Pond, please wake up.

583
00:45:22,260 --> 00:45:24,300
You have to come home with me.

584
00:45:25,120 --> 00:45:26,750
- Pond.
- Please help him.

585
00:45:34,860 --> 00:45:36,790
Now they can go home to their parents.

586
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:42,210
You died because of me.

587
00:45:46,140 --> 00:45:47,130
It's not your fault.

588
00:45:50,690 --> 00:45:52,090
It's my fault for making noise,

589
00:45:53,940 --> 00:45:55,670
and that got the kids hunted down.

590
00:45:56,680 --> 00:45:58,890
Master, please help him.

591
00:46:01,710 --> 00:46:03,650
You also ended up hurt.

592
00:46:24,360 --> 00:46:26,220
Baitong's health is delicate.

593
00:46:30,630 --> 00:46:34,860
Please pray for her
so she can deliver our baby safely.

594
00:46:50,770 --> 00:46:53,270
Master, can you please help him?

595
00:46:55,340 --> 00:46:56,950
Pond, please wake up.

596
00:46:56,980 --> 00:46:59,270
You have to come home with me.

597
00:47:07,990 --> 00:47:10,150
Pond, please wake up.

598
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:24,400
Thank you for giving your life to save Peem.

599
00:47:25,990 --> 00:47:27,730
Even though we never met,

600
00:47:29,400 --> 00:47:31,330
I will always dedicate merit to you.

601
00:47:39,580 --> 00:47:41,720
May the merit you have earned

602
00:47:41,980 --> 00:47:44,340
guide you to a better realm,

603
00:47:45,070 --> 00:47:46,420
where you find stillness,

604
00:47:46,710 --> 00:47:48,100
serenity, and peace,

605
00:47:49,560 --> 00:47:51,580
and may you leave this world
free of all worries.

606
00:48:03,110 --> 00:48:04,360
- That's enough.
- What?

607
00:48:04,390 --> 00:48:05,050
It hurts.

608
00:48:05,070 --> 00:48:06,860
Come on, bear with it, Master.

609
00:48:06,880 --> 00:48:08,190
This might be our last chance
to see each other.

610
00:48:12,170 --> 00:48:12,950
Yes?

611
00:48:13,190 --> 00:48:14,360
Are you jinxing me?

612
00:48:16,270 --> 00:48:17,190
Not at all.

613
00:48:22,660 --> 00:48:23,640
Hey, Charn.

614
00:48:24,190 --> 00:48:25,110
It's gorgeous over there.

615
00:48:25,140 --> 00:48:26,060
- Wanna take some photos?
- But...

616
00:48:26,090 --> 00:48:28,570
Over there. We can even feed the fish.

617
00:48:28,600 --> 00:48:29,520
Take a look.

618
00:48:29,950 --> 00:48:31,130
It's perfect, isn't it?

619
00:49:37,630 --> 00:49:39,290
Until the wedding,

620
00:49:41,330 --> 00:49:43,400
should I just stop you from taking any more jobs?

621
00:49:45,980 --> 00:49:48,180
Whenever you do, I can't reach you.

622
00:49:50,530 --> 00:49:52,330
If anything happens to you,

623
00:49:53,190 --> 00:49:54,510
how am I supposed to go on?

624
00:50:05,550 --> 00:50:06,700
I'm sorry.

625
00:50:14,360 --> 00:50:15,620
Whether it's now

626
00:50:17,110 --> 00:50:18,910
or after we're married,

627
00:50:20,620 --> 00:50:22,850
I'll tell you everything.

628
00:50:28,680 --> 00:50:30,300
If I ever have to save someone,

629
00:50:32,620 --> 00:50:34,000
I won't put my life on the line.

630
00:50:36,910 --> 00:50:38,680
I won't make you worry again.

631
00:50:53,230 --> 00:50:54,300
In this life,

632
00:50:56,940 --> 00:50:59,360
I will never let you be torn
from the one you love again.

633
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,460
And in this life,

634
00:51:12,580 --> 00:51:14,160
you won't be lonely,

635
00:51:16,810 --> 00:51:19,180
nor will you have to bear
the pain alone, either.

636
00:51:33,300 --> 00:51:35,390
No more risking your life like that.

637
00:52:41,720 --> 00:52:43,980
Keep moving, everybody.

638
00:52:53,590 --> 00:52:55,820
Keep going, everybody.

639
00:52:55,840 --> 00:52:57,130
Show them what you've got!

640
00:53:00,360 --> 00:53:01,000
Hey.

641
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:02,470
Jet.

642
00:53:02,500 --> 00:53:04,400
Hold it steady,
or you'll drop the betrothal tray.

643
00:53:04,420 --> 00:53:06,860
Can't help it.
These hips move faster than 5G internet.

644
00:53:06,880 --> 00:53:09,340
Once the beat drops,
they automatically sync up!

645
00:53:10,380 --> 00:53:11,320
I know

646
00:53:11,880 --> 00:53:15,000
my disciple can tell
what's proper and what's not.

647
00:53:17,320 --> 00:53:19,170
Yes, desynced now.

648
00:54:11,050 --> 00:54:12,190
All done.

649
00:54:13,080 --> 00:54:14,600
You look gorgeous, Khem.

650
00:54:15,110 --> 00:54:16,120
Khem,

651
00:54:17,410 --> 00:54:18,580
someone's here to see you.

652
00:54:44,230 --> 00:54:45,080
Father...

653
00:54:47,750 --> 00:54:48,830
How do I look?

654
00:54:49,990 --> 00:54:51,600
You look wonderful, my son.

655
00:55:04,650 --> 00:55:05,680
Khem.

656
00:55:06,790 --> 00:55:08,570
Your groom is here.

657
00:56:10,320 --> 00:56:13,740
At long last, we're finally one family.

658
00:56:14,760 --> 00:56:16,560
I love you more than anything, Khem.

659
00:56:17,000 --> 00:56:19,230
I love you, too.
More than anything in the world.

660
00:56:22,680 --> 00:56:23,470
Mom,

661
00:56:23,540 --> 00:56:25,750
would it be okay
if I stayed in Bangkok with Charn

662
00:56:25,770 --> 00:56:27,200
for about a month?

663
00:56:27,710 --> 00:56:29,450
Every time I wake up, he's already gone.

664
00:56:29,550 --> 00:56:31,400
You should clear things up with him.

665
00:56:31,740 --> 00:56:34,150
Once this task's done,
you'll have another one lined up.

666
00:56:34,290 --> 00:56:35,840
When will you ever have time for me?

667
00:56:37,240 --> 00:56:39,880
When I think about
how things might never be the same

668
00:56:40,210 --> 00:56:41,820
for the four of us,

669
00:56:42,790 --> 00:56:44,180
it breaks my heart.

670
00:56:46,630 --> 00:56:52,490
♪ I'm certain our paths were meant to align ♪

671
00:56:52,590 --> 00:56:57,860
♪ Fate brought you here to stand by my side ♪

672
00:56:57,880 --> 00:57:03,740
♪ And bound our love
to last till the end of time ♪

673
00:57:03,760 --> 00:57:06,990
♪ You're the blessing fate bestowed on me, ♪

674
00:57:07,010 --> 00:57:09,960
♪ My soulmate for eternity, ♪

675
00:57:09,990 --> 00:57:13,610
♪ Forever and endlessly ♪

676
00:57:26,060 --> 00:57:29,230
♪ You're the blessing fate bestowed on me, ♪

677
00:57:29,260 --> 00:57:32,260
♪ My soulmate for eternity, ♪

678
00:57:32,280 --> 00:57:36,280
♪ Forever and endlessly ♪

679
00:57:36,310 --> 00:57:38,290
[The UNCUT version of Khemjira Forever]

680
00:57:38,310 --> 00:57:40,180
[is exclusively available
on iQIYI and iQ.com]
